{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>The flesh.</b> Peshat. That is, after the flesh was sufficient to be absorbed, so that they should not say: He struck them only because He did not have the ability to provide what they asked. And it is stated in Midrash Tehillim regarding ״ויהרוג במשמניהם״ — that is, the fat ones and the healthy ones, who asked improperly out of a full belly; but the thin ones could have said that they were asking in order to make themselves healthy. And it is stated in chapter 2 of Ketubot: it is written ״הבשר עודנו בין שניהם״ and it is written ״עד חדש ימים״. How so? The average ones are judged immediately; the wicked suffer for thirty days."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:18.837973939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}